  "content": {
    "id": "p9-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Determine whether the following numbers are prime or composite using the primality test:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 4,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p9-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$151$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Prime.",
          "worked": "Since $12^2<151<13^2$, test the primes $2,3,5,7,11$. Neither $2$ nor $5$ divides $151$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}151&=3\\times50+1\\\\151&=7\\times21+4\\\\151&=11\\times13+8\\end{align*}$$\n\nNone of the required primes divides $151$, so $151$ is prime.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 100
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$169$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Composite.",
          "worked": "$\\sqrt{169}=13$, so $13$ is among the primes to test.\n\n$$169=13\\times13.$$\n\nThus $169$ has a prime divisor no greater than its square root and is composite.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 84
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q8-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$203$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Composite.",
          "worked": "Since $14^2<203<15^2$, $7$ is among the primes to test.\n\n$$203=7\\times29.$$\n\nThus $203$ has a prime divisor no greater than its square root and is composite.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 92
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q8-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$223$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Prime.",
          "worked": "Since $14^2<223<15^2$, test the primes $2,3,5,7,11,13$. Neither $2$ nor $5$ divides $223$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}223&=3\\times74+1\\\\223&=7\\times31+6\\\\223&=11\\times20+3\\\\223&=13\\times17+2\\end{align*}$$\n\nNone of the required primes divides $223$, so $223$ is prime.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 116
      }
    ]
  },
